rados es 4,8, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,2 a 7,2. En diciembre se adjudicó el 2 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 9 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 44 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.900 euros, se adjudicó en noviembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos cerca del límite no implica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones como la necesidad de un servicio o a precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar cuántos contratos se adjudicaron en diciembre y si algunos se repiten con el mismo adjudicatario. También se puede revisar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 52 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 10.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.2 to 7.2. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 9% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 44 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,900 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices might be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical patterns don't always mean improper actions.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same need. Review the awardee A's contracts for repeated purchases. Look at the December contracts to see if they fit a pattern. Contract [1] could be a starting point for further analysis.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","ci